9c8ab444 (1219 1793365948237 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f389") (src . "context: the users of the unit's names, and a provisional id refused as one\n\ncontext --for a code block listed none of the users of the definitions\nit holds: step 4's dependents are the blocks resting on T's hard\npremises, not the blocks that use T's names, so a definition called\nfrom two other files answered (dependents 0). context gains a soft\nclause of its own after background, (users (listed k) (of n) [(skipped\n...)] (user <id> (name ..) (library ..) (mode ..)) ...): for each name a\nblock of T's unit defines, the live code blocks outside the unit that\nuse it, by the name-use table uses reads, the view's own (the working\nview with --working), ordered by name then id. Users are admitted after\nthe dependents and before the relevant blocks, each whole or counted\nunder the excluded counter users. The clause is reserved at the\ncounters' digits whatever its counts are, so which hard blocks are\nshown, and at which level, still depends on nothing but the five\nqueries' rows, the hard records and the request; a count above the cap\nis shown at it with (capped), as the excluded counters show theirs. The\nfive queries, the receipt and the notes are unchanged. The human\nrendering prints the clause with its counts and one line per user.\n\nA draft new file's provisional id (new- and 56 hex digits), asked as a\nblock, was answered unknown-id with nearest ids. It names no block until\na commit makes one, so every verb that resolves an id over a view now\nanswers (error provisional-id (id ..) (reason not-committed)) from one\nconstructor in reduce.sc, called by rpc's unknown-id and by working-read;\nwith --working, a refusal of the view still comes first.\n\nTests: test/context-users.sc (39 rows: the users of one block and of a\nfile, the unit's own uses left out, the working view's table, the\nbudget's order and the invariant under a soft count elsewhere, the\ncounts at and above the cap, the provisional id through context, read\n--working, names and uses --under, and the exact shape); context-human\nand context-stale's differential rows leave the clause and the used\nnumber out of their comparison; change-stream-guard-expect lists the\ncontext answer; rows-baseline follows the fixtures.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 545))))
