66c89183 (1238 1793381587546 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f396") (src . "test: the scan-cost row reads medians over three pairs, and the two-opener daemon rows read the held loser by pid\n\nTwo fixture rows went red on the CI runner (3 vCPU, the suite in\nparallel) and never on the development machine, and each was a row\nwhose single reading could not tell a slow scanner from a busy host.\n\necmascript-scan A8 timed one pair of scans, N lines and 4N lines, and\nasked the 4N scan to take at most 6 times the N scan. One pair is one\nsample: on the runner it read 6.71 once and 4.45 on the rerun of the\nsame tree, while a quadratic scanner reads 13 times here. The row now\ntimes three alternating pairs (N, 4N, N, 4N, N, 4N) and compares the\nmedian of the 4N readings with 6 times the median of the N readings,\nfloored at 1 ms; a comment beside it says why the median and not the\nworst pair (one stalled pair is the host, three slow pairs are the\nscanner). The times and the medians are printed as readings.\n\ndaemon-idle Q19 raced two openers on a fresh run root and read the\nserve log and a process count after the race; the loser's serve-busy\nline is written by its own daemon after the row had read the log, so\nthe count was read against an exiting process. The rows now hold each\nopener's daemon before its report write (a per-opener report-write\nhold beside the opener-after-probe hold), read both openers ready with\none hold reached and no serve-busy line yet, release the loser and wait\non its pid, then read exactly one serve-busy refusal carrying the\nloser's attempt token, the surviving daemon by pid equal to the winner,\nthe endpoint link still the winner's, and a connection accepted. Rows\nread by pid, not by count: a mutant that leaves the winner dead and a\nstray daemon alive read green on the counted rows and red on these.\n\nMutants read red on the new rows and nothing else: a quadratic scanner,\na scanner with one stall, a daemon that answers ready without starting,\none that writes no serve-busy report, and one that kills the winner.\nrows-baseline.txt carries the two fixtures' new hashes and counts.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 549))))
